! Every wiggler in the line tracked unaveraged, selected on the elements themselves.
! The default 2-period ramps carry two priced end effects (the manual's unaveraged-mode
! section): their slippage deficit is compensated exactly by the mode's built-in phase
! jump, and their reduced coupling length costs about 2% in ln power per segment. Both
! are field physics of adiabatic ends rather than something hidden.

call, file = aramis.bmad
wiggler::*[TRACKING_METHOD] = fel_unaveraged
